:name: U400 boot under the Thread/Matter ground-truth environment
:description: Boots the Aqara U400 Aliro firmware inside the EXACT same platform/bridge setup used by the working Thread/Matter e2e scenarios (brd2601b.repl + phase3-bridges.repl + BLE/802.15.4 mediums), instead of the standalone boot_mg24.resc harness, to see whether the radio-init spin behaves differently with the bridges connected.
# Mirrors matter/renode-thread/scenarios/e2e-15.4-fragrx.resc structure; only the ELF + vector table differ.

mach create "stock"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd2601b.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @matter/renode-thread/scenarios/phase3-bridges.repl
sysbus LoadELF @matter/aliro-u400/firmware/U400_primary_target.elf
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08006000
cpu PerformanceInMips 39
seqcpu PerformanceInMips 39
emulation CreateBLEMedium "wireless"
connector Connect sysbus.radio wireless
connector Connect sysbus.bleCentral wireless
connector Connect sysbus.ieee802154 wireless
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
emulation SetGlobalAdvanceImmediately false
logFile @/tmp/u400-threadenv.log true
logLevel 2
logLevel 1 sysbus.radio

emulation RunFor "3.0"
pause

echo ">>> PC after 3s (compare to standalone-harness result 0x808105c):"
sysbus.cpu PC
echo ">>> instruction at that PC:"
sysbus ReadWord `sysbus.cpu PC`
quit
